title: Chancellor [+ chancellor +] replaced by Franz von Papen
subtitle: President Hindenburg dismisses the government.
view-if: (chancellor = "Brüning" or chancellor = "Wirth" or chancellor = "Adenauer") and ((year = 1932 and month >= 5) or year >= 1933) and president = "Hindenburg" and z_in_government = 1 and hindenburg_relation <= 1 
on-arrival: old_chancellor = chancellor; spd_toleration = 0; chancellor = "Papen"; chancellor_party = "I"; next_election_time = time+3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; judicial_reform -= 2 if judicial_reform >= 2; finance_minister_party = "I"; interior_minister_party = "I"; economy_minister_party = "I"; labor_minister_party = "I"; foreign_minister_party = "I"; agriculture_minister_party = "I"; reichswehr_minister = "I";
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/portraits/PapenFranz.jpg

Due to our recent actions facing their displeasure, President Hindenburg's secretive group of advisors (often called the "camarilla") has turned against [+ old_chancellor +], and Hindenburg his dismissed the Chancellor, replacing him with Franz von Papen! 

Papen is immediately faced with a vote of no confidence, given his unpopularity. However we vote, he is guaranteed to fall, due to the unanimous hatred against him from all other parties. [? if z_party_leader = "Kaas" : Not that Ludwig Kaas would ever allow any member of his party to vote confidence in his archenemy. ?] Meanwhile, he is governing via emergency powers with Hindenburg. His first policy is to legalize the Nazi SA, but this does not win their loyalty.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
